# Configuration Parameters (SystemC CCI)

Runtime configuration for any SystemC/TLM model in this repository must go through the
**Accellera CCI 1.0** API (`cci::cci_param`), not ad-hoc globals, environment
variables, or hand-rolled config structs alone. CCI gives every model the same
broker-mediated, introspectable, preset-overridable parameter surface.

## Scope

- **Hand-written models** (any subsystem — SMC, SEP, VP, fabric, CPU cluster,
  and future models): declare parameters as `cci::cci_param<T>` members, or
  as `regmodel::Param<T>` from `common/include/reg_param.h` (SEP's CCI
  wrapper with INI / vector-as-JSON helpers). Do not add parallel knobs
  for the same setting.
- A legacy `*_cfg` struct may remain for constructor defaults, but new
  tunables must also be exposed as CCI parameters (Phase-1 migration pattern
  in `smc/cpu_cluster/doc/04_CCI_Integration_Guide.md`).

`#include <cci_configuration>` and link the target against `SystemC::cci`.

## Declaring parameters

```cpp
// In the module class — declare BEFORE ports / sized members / FIFOs so
// member-init order resolves presets before sizing.
cci::cci_param<unsigned, cci::CCI_IMMUTABLE_PARAM> num_harts_p_;
cci::cci_param<double>                             access_delay_ns_p_;

// In the constructor initializer list — short relative name, default, description.
num_harts_p_("num_harts", cfg.num_harts,
             "Number of harts (1..4095). Sizes msip_o[] / mtip_o[].")
, access_delay_ns_p_("access_delay_ns", 2.0,
                    "TLM register-access annotated delay (ns). Mutable at run-time.")
```

Conventions:

- Member suffix `_p_`; CCI name is the short leaf (`"num_harts"`, not the full
  hierarchical path — CCI prepends the module hierarchy automatically).
- **Immutable** (`cci::CCI_IMMUTABLE_PARAM`) for sizing/structural knobs (array
  depths, port counts, clock periods) that cannot change after elaboration.
- **Mutable** (plain `cci::cci_param<T>`) for run-time tunables (`access_delay_ns`,
  `quantum_ns`, feature flags). Re-read `.get_value()` when used (e.g. each
  `b_transport`), do not cache once at construction.
- Add `add_metadata()` for timing params (`"unit"` → `"nanoseconds"`,
  `"tlm_phase"` → `"annotated_delay"`).

## Broker setup (platforms and testbenches)

Register the global broker **before any** `cci_param` is constructed:

```cpp
#include <cci/utils/consuming_broker.h>

int sc_main(int, char**) {
    cci::cci_register_broker(new cci_utils::consuming_broker("GlobalBroker"));

    cci::cci_originator platform_cfg("platform_cfg");
    auto broker = cci::cci_get_global_broker(platform_cfg);
    broker.set_preset_cci_value("tb.plic.num_sources", cci::cci_value(64u));

    tb top("tb");   // DUT picks up presets during construction
    sc_core::sc_start();
}
```

- Preset keys use the **full hierarchical name** (`"tb.plic.num_sources"`).
- Inside the SystemC hierarchy, use `cci::cci_get_broker()` (no originator).
- Testbench sizing params that mirror the DUT must receive matching presets so
  `sc_vector` widths stay consistent (see `plic_tb.cpp`).

## Do not

- Introduce new model knobs as bare constructor arguments, `static` globals,
  or `getenv()` reads when CCI is available.
- Mark sizing parameters mutable — changing them post-elaboration breaks port
  bindings and scheduled events.
- Access another module's `cci_param` member directly; use broker handles
  (`broker.get_param_handle("module.param")`).

See `smc/cpu_cluster/doc/04_CCI_Integration_Guide.md` for broker concepts,
callbacks, introspection, and migration from legacy `config` structs.
